{"replay": "text", "text": "## What I changed\n\nThe reader now stops at the first value it cannot convert and says which line it was on, instead of handing a zero to the rest of the module.\n\n- `Reader.convert` throws `ReaderError.badValue(line:)`\n- the callers in `Config` and `Import` pass the error on\n- two tests cover a bad value at the start and at the end\n\n### Why\n\nA zero looked like a real value, so the sums further down came out wrong without any sign of where it started. Stopping at the bad value points straight at the line to fix.\n\n```swift\nlet value = try Reader.convert(raw, as: .number)\n```\n\nEverything builds and the tests pass.", "chunk": 400, "ms": 1}
